WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.620
Now that Disney+'s Mandalorian has introduced
a mysterious new character that bears more

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.380
than a passing resemblance to the Jedi master
Yoda, it got us thinking: What's up with this

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.180
species of pint-sized, pointy-eared aliens?

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.820
What makes them so special, and what have
we learned about them over the years?

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.320
In a Moviefone interview between George Lucas
and Hayden Christensen where they answered

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:28.120
fan questions, Lucas was asked about Yoda's
species and his off-screen history.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.920
Lucas described Yoda as:

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.380
"A mystery character, a magical character,
he has no background, he comes and he goes,

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.280
he's the subversive, secret, mysterious stranger."

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.380
As the years went on and the Expanded Universe
was created, Lucas still didn't want anyone

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.320
to give Yoda any kind of backstory.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.160
He eventually added another character of Yoda's
species to The Phantom Menace more on her

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.960
in a bit and let creators in the Expanded
Universe invent a couple more of the same

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:56.500
species.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.580
But when Lucas sold Star Wars to Disney, everything
in the Expanded Universe was considered non-canon,

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.960
leaving only three Yoda-like characters in
the Star Wars universe.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.710
While there have been several of Yoda's species,
including those from the Extended Universe

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:15.820
and the Knights of the Old Republic video
game, at this point in time, there are only

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:21.870
three in the official Star Wars canon: Yoda,
Yaddle, and this new "Child" character colloquially

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.820
known to fans as "Baby Yoda."

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.700
Yoda, of course, is the most visible of his
species, appearing in six films, as well as

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.340
in the animated shows Star Wars Rebels and
Star Wars: The Clone Wars.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.840
"Last time, I couldn't see you."

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.580
"Ahh, growing, your abilities are."

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.820
Yaddle, a female of the Yoda species, was
seen in The Phantom Menace.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.360
She was a Jedi Master and a member of the
Jedi High Council alongside Yoda.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:52.210
Yaddle was there when Qui-Gon Jinn brought
a young Anakin Skywalker to be evaluated by

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.640
the Jedi High Council.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.021
However, after the Battle of Naboo, Yaddle
wanted a break from the Jedi Council, and

00:01:58.021 --> 00:02:00.580
she was already gone when The Clone Wars began
to air.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.200
As the Child has only recently been introduced
to us in The Mandalorian, there's very little

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.520
information known about it.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.820
We know it's approximately 50 years old, and
that it's strong with the Force.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.200
We also know it tried to help the bounty hunter
heal his wounds.

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:19.220
The only other thing we know about baby Yoda
right now is that it has captured our hearts,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.350
and it must be protected at all costs.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:28.370
According to StarWars.com, the Force is, quote,
"a mysterious energy field created by life

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.980
that binds the galaxy together."

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:35.200
The Jedi, the Sith, and other Force-sensitive
beings "harness the power of the Force," giving

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.830
them amazing abilities such as "levitating
objects, tricking minds, and seeing things

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.820
before they happen."

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:44.980
And as you probably guessed, the Yoda species
is strong with the Force.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.620
Yoda is seen using it several times throughout
the Star Wars franchise.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:52.740
The first time we see him use it is in The
Empire Strikes Back when training Luke.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.680
After Skywalker fails to lift his X-wing out
of the bottom of the swamp, Yoda shows him

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:01.400
that it is indeed possible to use the Force
to lift something so heavy.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.660
We were also blessed to see Baby Yoda use
the Force in the second episode of The Mandalorian.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.390
In the scene, the bounty hunter is being attacked
by a giant alien after stealing an egg from

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.380
the creature's cave.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.820
Just when it looks like he's done for, Baby
Yoda reaches out and lifts the monster into

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.100
the air, allowing the bounty hunter to grab
his knife and kill it.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.260
Lifting that monster took everything out of
Baby Yoda, though, and he went night-night

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.860
for a long while afterwards.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:32.060
In The Mandalorian, when the title hero and
IG-11 realize the target they're looking for

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.380
is actually Baby Yoda, the bounty hunter says,
quote, "Wait.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:37.780
They said 50 years old."

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.320
IG-11 then tells him, quote, "Species age
differently.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.510
Perhaps it could live many centuries."

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:48.500
So if baby Yoda is 50 years old, that would
place him being born around the same time

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.620
as Anakin Skywalker.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.380
After all, The Mandalorian takes place five
years after Return of the Jedi, the film in

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.380
which Yoda dies.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.680
We know that Yoda was approximately 900 years
old at the time of his death.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:05.480
Around the age of 100, Yoda had already become
a Jedi Master and had begun training apprentices.

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:11.160
When he died, it was thought Yoda had taught
over 20,000 Jedi, including Count Dooku and,

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.860
of course, Luke Skywalker.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:17.180
There still is a bit of mystery when it comes
to just how long Yoda's species lives because

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:23.050
both Yoda and Yaddle who, in the non-canon
Expanded Universe, was 483 years old at the

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:27.319
time of her death were Jedi, and it's thought
they could live longer than an average member

00:04:27.319 --> 00:04:28.319
of the species.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:34.210
In case there was any doubt, Baby Yoda made
it perfectly clear in episode two of The Mandalorian

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.200
that his species definitely eats meat.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.600
He catches a rather large, frog-like creature
and swallows it whole.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.370
Although we don't really see Yoda eating during
any of his appearances well, other than stealing

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:49.300
a bite of Luke's dinner it was thought his
species were carnivores due to the shape of

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:49.940
their teeth.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:52.160
"Ooh!"

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.140
"Put that down.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:54.860
We — Hey!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:56.640
That's my dinner!"

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:02.619
Yoda's chompers are super sharp, like razors,
which can make quick work of ripping and chewing

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:03.880
the skin of an animal.

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:08.240
Those large claws on the end of their three
fingers also come into play, making it easy

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.880
to stab their potential meal.

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:13.220
We know Yoda was eating vegetables while living
on Dagobah, though.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.440
On the day Luke came to the swamp planet,
the tiny alien was making something called

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.340
rootleaf stew.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:23.100
Made of yarum and galla seeds, with some mushroom
spores tossed in for good measure, this was

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:25.000
part of Yoda's diet while exiled.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:30.460
Whether all of the Yoda species also eat vegetables
isn't known, but this makes Yoda himself an

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.060
omnivore.

